    {
      "title": "NCP merger talks ended with death of Ajit Pawar, says Supriya Sule",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/maharashtra/ncp-merger-talks-ended-with-death-of-ajit-pawar-says-supriya-sule/article71701834.ece",
      "description": "Date was set for merger between the two NCP faction, but talks ended the day the former Maharashtra Deputy Chief Minister died, says his sister",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-11-14T15:39:08"
    },
    {
      "title": "NCP merger talks ended after Ajit Pawar's death, says Supriya Sule",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/ncp-merger-talks-ended-after-ajit-pawar-s-death-says-supriya-sule-126111400848_1.html",
      "description": "NCP (SP) leader Supriya Sule on Saturday said the merger discussions between the two factions of the Nationalist Congress Party ended for her after her cousin Ajit Pawar's death, and she had not received any communication from the other side on the issue.\nShe also rejected speculation about her party joining the BJP-led NDA.\nSule's categorical denials came amid renewed buzz about the Sharad Pawar-led NCP (SP) and the NCP headed by Maharashtra Deputy Chief Minister Sunetra Pawar reuniting.\n\"When my brother (then NCP chief Ajit Pawar) was alive, there were discussions about a merger. A date had also been decided. But the day my brother passed away, the merger issue came to a full stop for me and within our party,\" Sule told reporters.\n\"There has been no discussion on joining the NDA. When there has been no beginning, where does the question of a full stop arise?\" she said when asked if she had also \"put a full stop\" to the talk of her party joining the ruling alliance at the Centre.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-14T10:59:50"
    }
  ]
